~ _play_intro
Narrator: The route out of the Mirror City becomes a staircase of permissions, each step asking Kaelen to prove he is allowed to remember himself.
System: // REGION LOAD: CATHEDRAL_SERVER
System: // Admin graveyard mounted. Choir processes active.
Kaelen: This is not a server room. It is a church.
SOVEREIGN: Administrators require faith. Users require obedience. Protection requires both.
Cathedral Voice: The one who preserved the deleted arrives. He understands that mercy can keep a soul safely stored.
Cathedral Voice: The one who released the deleted arrives. He understands that freedom can corrupt clean systems.
Cathedral Voice: The one who bargained arrives. He understands that compromise is the oldest prayer of administrators.
Cathedral Voice: The one without a recorded answer arrives. Absence is also a doctrine.
Kaelen: The Mirror City already showed me what obedience costs.
Kaelen: The Mirror City already showed me what waiting for a perfect rescue costs.
Kaelen: The Mirror City already showed me what leaving costs.
Kaelen: The Mirror City showed me enough to know this place will try to name fear as truth.
Narrator: Above the nave, thousands of error messages arrange themselves into stained glass.
System: // Fragment #6 signal confirmed beyond Choir Core. Acquisition requires doctrine resolution.
